<span style="color: red;">INTERPRETATION #1: How many chloroplast and/or mitochondrial ASVs in your dataset? Does this seem reasonable?</span>
A total of 227 ASVs were removed as chloroplast and/or mitochondrial sequences, because the dataset decreased from 8788 taxa in the raw phyloseq object to 8561 taxa after chloroplast and mitochondrial filtering. This seems reasonable for a host-associated 16S dataset, since mitochondria and chloroplast sequences can be unintentionally amplified along with bacterial 16S targets. Removing these ASVs should improve the biological accuracy of the downstream microbial community analysis.
<span style="color: red;">INTERPRETATION #1: How many chloroplast and/or mitochondrial ASVs in your dataset? Does this seem reasonable?</span>
# How many total asvs were removed from chloros and mitos?
ntaxa(raw_physeq) - ntaxa(noChlorosMitos_physeq)
# proportion of asvs kept?
ntaxa(noChlorosMitos_physeq)/ntaxa(raw_physeq)
library(phyloseq)
library(iNEXT)
library(tidyverse)
# Load your preprocessed phyloseq object
load("data/03_PreProcessing/preprocessed_physeq.RData")
# Make sure output folder exists
dir.create("data/04_Biodiversity", recursive = TRUE, showWarnings = FALSE)
# Prepare iNEXT input
# iNEXT wants ASVs/species in rows and samples in columns
otu_mat <- as(otu_table(preprocessed_physeq), "matrix")
if(!taxa_are_rows(preprocessed_physeq)){
otu_mat <- t(otu_mat)
}
iNEXT_input_df <- as.data.frame(otu_mat)
# Quick checks
dim(iNEXT_input_df)
iNEXT_input_df[1:5, 1:5]
# Set seed for reproducibility
set.seed(238428)
# Run iNEXT
iNEXT_data <- iNEXT(
iNEXT_input_df,
q = c(0, 1, 2),
datatype = "abundance"
)
# Save for later
save(iNEXT_data, file = "data/04_Biodiversity/iNEXT_data.RData")
# Optional quick check
str(iNEXT_data, max.level = 1)
j
dim(iNEXT_input_df)
typeof(iNEXT_data)
